# estige relay node — Oracle Linux package env file.
#
# Read by systemd's EnvironmentFile= for estige-relay.service. Mode 0600
# root:root. This role never reads VPN_OPERATOR_KEYS; the exit node never reads
# VPN_OPERATOR_TOKEN (docs/d090's disjoint credentials).
#
# The exit node this relay dials, and the shared secret (docs/d104).
# Single-quote a token carrying shell metacharacters.
# VPN_TUNNEL_URL=https://vpn.example.test/vpn
# VPN_OPERATOR_TOKEN='<token>'
#
# Optional deployment label carried in the HELLO (docs/d090).
# VPN_CLIENT_LABEL=
#
# The relay's own upstream chain (docs/d094), if it must egress through
# another proxy. Leave unset for a direct dial. These samples deliberately
# name another host: a value naming THIS relay's listeners is refused as a
# self-chain (exit 94). Conventional names:
# SOCKS_SERVER=proxy.example.test:1080
# SOCKS_VERSION=5
# HTTP_PROXY=http://proxy.example.test:3128
# HTTPS_PROXY=http://proxy.example.test:3128
# ALL_PROXY=http://proxy.example.test:3128
